Z||000000||fiero56||08-24-2000||02:11 PM||||This is from the e-groups Fiero list, but felt it belonged here too.<P><BR>I just spoke with Bob Parker, our host for the NEFA Fiero swap meet this<BR>weekend. Last night, Bob's garage burned down. This is not his barn with<BR>all the Fiero parts but it is the garage where he works on the cars and<BR>other things. Lost in the blaze were Bob's 2 Huey helicopters (which he<BR>was trying to built one running one from) plus a plane and all histools.<BR>When I spoke with him he was waiting for the insurance company to call.<BR>Please don't call unless you want parts as Bob is a bit preoccupiedright now.<BR>But Bob (and Holly) are troopers and say that the weekend goes on as<BR>planned It does throw a damper on things but lets rise above it. A great<BR>weekend will provide an excellent moral boost.<BR>See you Saturday.... despite the disaster, this is going to be sooooo<BR>cool! I've spoken with a lot of people. Seems everyone is bringing<BR>something to sell or trade.Ray PaulkNew England Fiero Association, President<BR>Mid-Atlantic Fiero Owners Association, Director--<BR>This list is proudly sponsored by:<BR>The Fiero Factory - 8710B Hwy 53, Toney, AL 35773<BR>Parts, Service, Fieros for sale! - <A HREF="http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory" TARGET=_blank>http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory</A> <BR>Days: 256-420-5391    Nites: 256-882-1568<BR>List Moderator:  FIERO-owner@egroups.com<BR>Unsubscribe:     FIERO-unsubscribe@egroups.com||||reg||1
